{"title":"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Law_of_Cosines)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Law of Cosines)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Similar_Triangles)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Similar Triangles)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. If \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/524032b85d24eb1319dff54cd13c53fba0331c9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CAD} = \\angle{DAB} = 60^\\circ\\mbox{, }AC = 3\\mbox{ and }AB = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"357\" height=\"16\" />, \nthen the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/0/5d0d5b83bc4785302710c0292279ac70c5b7a08d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} \\ 2 \\qquad  \\textbf{(B)} \\ 2.5 \\qquad  \\textbf{(C)} \\ 3 \\qquad  \\textbf{(D)} \\ 3.5 \\qquad  \\textbf{(E)} \\ 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"377\" height=\"17\" />   \n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Law_of_Cosines.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Law_of_Cosines)\">Solution 1 (Law of Cosines)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Law of Cosines)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/3/4439ef25674b53561f74b5a6674c7d85cbc74ad0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> bisects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/2/2e2c830e136e667485791216de260e10db2c2195.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{BAC}$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" />, the Angle Bisector Theorem gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/0/0a078ba5b9df19170bf0aed4111215fb21fa8588.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{DB}{CD} = \\frac{AB}{AC} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"123\" height=\"38\" />, so let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/4/604d2fb7d65192ae3919926f921e7078a5473dd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = x$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/c/a4cf45c832f65bdfcc439908b0e589b9e5cbf545.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DB = 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" />. Applying the Law of Cosines to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/8/fc8f59495796eb4b2416631af1682f18bfcfbf35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CAD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/b/a3bc4b06e12604cb763d346833d143f2de466c89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 = 3^2 + y^2 - 3y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"20\" />, and to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/e/8be25cedbf9b65c5d6d74dc50e886682a0778627.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DAB$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/c/c8c9a6946ae0710603534336b1083811325031d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2x)^2 = 6^2 + y^2 - 6y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"161\" height=\"19\" />. Subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times the first equation from the second equation therefore yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/1/1b1fb0e0fd85233685f960ce3b2b34a8b909926c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 = 6y - 3y^2 \\Rightarrow y(y-2) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"226\" height=\"19\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. But since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/8/5c8eb2cb0cf3c53328e172b4cf6f48f09f2f8e9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is the length of a side of a triangle), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/f/4bf5d3494fa11e29262bf2d58d7d5d45d5b1b12b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)} \\ 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Similar_Triangles.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Similar_Triangles)\">Solution 2 (Similar Triangles)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Similar Triangles)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a point on line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/8/a58ef1a0b89bdd01d9afe0e65f59fbdf3e144198.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/9057d4d264f5530ac63d366089bc3c17ce5d79a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> must be equilateral, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/d/0eddb9899b4eca747bab5d1c65ade51a139508a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/5/ab5c2299384f586cc910619ac0bd0547cf8ae1e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BEC = 60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" />.  So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/5/ae5fbef2b5901dd2fadce6387cbfbf5d45ec1cb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE \\parallel DA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/c/3dcc158cbe05c253bb3122b28f476d874c96c221.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CDA \\sim \\triangle CBE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" />.  So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/d/1bdafeab37aff312b717dc15706b373a19011654.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AD}{6} = \\frac{3}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"72\" height=\"39\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/f/a6fcf5da9d26f2738948a48ed8fa422893a96d05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = \\boxed{(\\mathbf{A})\\ 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"111\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>-j314andrews\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME\" title=\"1983 AHSME\">1983 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1983 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1983\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspa